<figure class="mcp-flow" aria-labelledby="mcp-flow-title" aria-describedby="mcp-flow-description">
  <figcaption id="mcp-flow-title">How OpenShift Lightspeed uses MCP Gateway</figcaption>
  <p id="mcp-flow-description" class="mcp-flow__intro">
    Both requests enter the same Gateway endpoint. The JSON-RPC method determines the path through the Gateway.
  </p>

  <div class="mcp-flow__entry" aria-label="OpenShift Lightspeed sends an MCP request to Envoy at the gateway endpoint">
    <div class="mcp-flow__node mcp-flow__node--client">
      <span class="mcp-flow__eyebrow">MCP client</span>
      <strong>OpenShift Lightspeed</strong>
      <small>Sends an MCP request to <code>/mcp</code></small>
    </div>
    <span class="mcp-flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    <div class="mcp-flow__node mcp-flow__node--gateway">
      <span class="mcp-flow__eyebrow">One entry point</span>
      <strong>MCP Gateway</strong>
      <small class="mcp-flow__request">
        <span>Envoy receives the request</span>
        <code>Gateway endpoint: /mcp</code>
      </small>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mcp-flow__branch" aria-hidden="true">
    <span></span>
    <b>method?</b>
    <span></span>
  </div>

  <ol class="mcp-flow__paths">
    <li class="mcp-flow__path mcp-flow__path--list">
      <header>
        <span class="mcp-flow__path-number">1</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Discover available tools</strong>
          <code>tools/list</code>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="mcp-flow__steps">
        <div class="mcp-flow__step">
          <span>Router</span>
          <strong>Reads the method</strong>
          <small>Keeps the Gateway hostname</small>
        </div>
        <span class="mcp-flow__step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div class="mcp-flow__step mcp-flow__step--accent">
          <span>Broker</span>
          <strong>Builds the shared catalog</strong>
          <small>Reads registered tools and adds each server's prefix</small>
        </div>
        <span class="mcp-flow__step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div class="mcp-flow__step mcp-flow__step--result">
          <span>Result to Lightspeed</span>
          <strong><code>openshift_*</code></strong>
          <small>Names and descriptions of tools</small>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>The broker reads the backend tool list. No OpenShift tool runs.</p>
    </li>

    <li class="mcp-flow__path mcp-flow__path--call">
      <header>
        <span class="mcp-flow__path-number">2</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Run one selected tool</strong>
          <code>tools/call</code>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="mcp-flow__steps">
        <div class="mcp-flow__step">
          <span>Router</span>
          <strong>Maps the prefix</strong>
          <small>Removes <code>openshift_</code> and sets the backend host</small>
        </div>
        <span class="mcp-flow__step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div class="mcp-flow__step mcp-flow__step--accent">
          <span>Envoy + HTTPRoute</span>
          <strong>Select the Service</strong>
          <small><code>mcp-server-test:8080</code></small>
        </div>
        <span class="mcp-flow__step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div class="mcp-flow__step">
          <span>MCP server</span>
          <strong>Runs the tool</strong>
          <small>Calls the OpenShift API for this read-only experiment</small>
        </div>
        <span class="mcp-flow__step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <div class="mcp-flow__step mcp-flow__step--result">
          <span>OpenShift API</span>
          <strong>Returns permitted data</strong>
          <small>The tool result returns to Lightspeed</small>
        </div>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>
</figure>

